jobs.description:
Are you looking for a varied role in production? Do you enjoy taking responsibility and working as part of a team? If this sounds like you, then the role of Production Worker at Klaas Puul is perfect for you! Working for an organization that is recognized for its success? KP is one of the finalists in the North Holland Entrepreneur Awards 2026, a great recognition of our ambition, innovation, and entrepreneurial culture.



 Please note: only candidates who are currently living in the Netherlands can apply.

In this role, you will be involved in a variety of activities across logistics, production, and cleaning. You may assist with packaging our shrimp and other tasks that help maintain an efficient production process. Hygiene and safety are top priorities for us, and you will ensure that your work always meets these standards.

What you bring:

At Klaas Puul, we are looking for colleagues who fit into our growing company. You are ready to take on challenges with us and contribute to developing a new, shared company culture. You bring certain experience and skills that you can apply in this role:

  - MBO-level (intermediate vocational education) work and thinking skills;

  - 0–2 years of relevant work experience, preferably in a production or logistics environment;

  - You must live in the Netherlands; applications from abroad will not be considered;

  - Proactive, hygienic, precise, and a true team player;

  - Good verbal and written communication skills in English; Dutch is a plus;

  - Forklift certification is a plus;

  - Basic knowledge of food safety and familiarity with guidelines around food fraud and food defense, or a willingness to develop these skills further.

What we offer:

At Klaas Puul, you will work in an informal, dynamic environment with plenty of freedom and opportunities for personal development, including training and coaching. We believe that our success starts with happy employees, and we work together to help everyone per

Are you detail-oriented, quality-focused, and looking for a full-time job in a dynamic logistics environment? Then this opportunity as a Quality Control Employee in Lelystad could be the perfect fit for you!

As a Quality Control Employee, you play a key role in ensuring that products meet the highest quality standards before moving further through the logistics process. You will work in a supportive team environment and be part of a 2-shift schedule (morning and afternoon shifts)

As a Quality Control Employee, your responsibilities include:

- Inspecting products to ensure they meet quality standards;
- Identifying, reporting, and helping resolve product defects;
- Carefully checking products for damages, errors, or irregularities;
- Maintaining a clean and organized work area;
- Contributing to an efficient and high-quality logistics operation;
- Following quality and safety procedures at all times.

- Basic English communication skills are required;
- Full-time availability;
- Strong attention to detail and quality;
- Ability to work effectively in a team environment;
- Ability to follow instructions accurately;
- Previous experience in quality control, production, or logistics is an advantage, but not required.

As a C Driver, you are responsible for driving the truck and delivering a wide range of food and non-food products to customers such as restaurants, cafés, sports clubs, and company canteens. Together with your driver’s assistant, you handle loading and unloading and ensure deliveries are completed safely and efficiently.

This is an active role where you are frequently on the move and work in all weather conditions. You will primarily work from Monday to Friday, with regular shifts on Saturdays. Your start time is fixed, but flexibility is required regarding your finishing time.

At the start of the day, you review the route together, load the truck, and begin your deliveries. You also handle basic administrative tasks and provide friendly, customer-focused service. After completing your route, you return to the depot and check in for any additional assignments.

If you perform well, you will have the opportunity to obtain your CE license and grow within the company.

- Valid Category C driving licence and Code 95;
- In possession of a digital driver card;
- Own transport (car/moped/scooter/motorcycle);
- Experience as a driver;
- Living in the vicinity of Berkel en Rodenrijs;
- Presentable appearance;
- Available full-time and flexible;
- Good command of the English language, both spoken and written;

From the job description, you may have already noticed that this is a physically demanding role in which you do more than just drive the vehicle. It is therefore important that this suits you. If so, we encourage you to apply. Who knows, you might soon start working for our client.
